@prefix this: <http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/> .
@prefix sub: <http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/> .
@prefix np: <http://www.nanopub.org/nschema#> .
@prefix npx: <http://purl.org/nanopub/x/> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix dct: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix delphi: <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/> .

sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/genotype-developmental-ordering> a delphi:Concept, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "No structure develops from a precursor that appears later than it does (Lean 4, kernel-checked)" ;
    dct:description "Taking the developmental stage as the level of a graph whose edges are develops_from, a decidable check passes exactly when every edge goes strictly down in stage; then every derivative is staged after its precursor and the relation is acyclic." ;
    dct:source "Proved in this project (lean/Delphi/Favored.lean) as an extension of the neutral case of Kimura (1962) to non-opposing selection; no paper states it in this form." ;
    skos:notation "devOrderedB g = true  =>  (forall edges a b, level b < level a) and Acyclic" ;
    skos:definition """theorem devOrdered_of_check (g : Graph ℕ) (h : devOrderedB g = true) :
    (∀ a b, g.Edge a b → g.level b < g.level a) ∧ g.Acyclic"""^^delphi:lean4 ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    delphi:leanDeclaration "Delphi.Genotype.devOrderedB" ;
    delphi:leanTheorem "Delphi.Genotype.devOrdered_of_check", "Delphi.Genotype.devOrdered_acyclic" ;
    delphi:leanVerified "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    skos:scopeNote "The ZFIN stage-series ids are taken to order the stages. Nothing here is about the flying fish: the subtree is zebrafish anatomy joined to the blueprint by cross-references. An edge with an unknown stage is not certified, not passed." ;
    rdfs:comment "Status: kernel-checked (Lean 4 accepted the module with zero sorry and standard axioms only). Not expert-validated. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it; strict neutrality, constant population size, Wright-Fisher reproduction and independent mutant fates (Kimura), fixed fitnesses and haploid inheritance (Fisher), equal fecundity and a 1:1 sex ratio (Maynard Smith) are assumptions written in the module header, not conclusions. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the paper is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/Delphi/Genotype.lean>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/genotype-developmental-ordering> dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/genotype-developmental-ordering> ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-genotype-developmental-ordering> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-genotype-developmental-ordering> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Lean 4 kernel accepted Delphi.Genotype.devOrdered_of_check with zero sorry and standard axioms, and rejected 1 deliberately broken variant(s)" ;
    dct:description "Build receipt. Lean (version 4.35.0, x86_64-w64-windows-gnu, commit eb6cafb7290e8bd5f2937522d8d804f58f02bafc, Release); toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0; Mathlib v4.35.0 (56a005855ea17e0b0958f73ec801ae140b0a1679). lake build exit 0 in 23.2 s with 0 errors; 0 sorry in lean/Delphi/Genotype.lean (224 lines). #print axioms for Delphi.Genotype.devOrdered_of_check, Delphi.Genotype.devOrdered_acyclic: Quot.sound, propext only (Lean's standard axioms; no sorryAx). Mutation evidence (lean/mutate.mjs, 2026-10-31T21:58:20.213Z): 1 deliberate change(s) to the statement or the model were each rejected by the compiler: [dev-certificate-self-edge] Data sabotaged: a develops_from edge from a node to itself is added to the certified list, so something would develop from itself and no stage could be strictly earlier. The kernel-evaluated checker must reject it. Rejected with 1 error(s): FinDevelopment.lean:18:55: error: Tactic `decide` proved that the proposition Controls: 16 of 16 unmodified modules accepted by the same command." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/genotype-developmental-ordering> ;
    rdfs:comment "This evidence item establishes that the stated theorem follows from the stated model. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it; strict neutrality, constant population size, Wright-Fisher reproduction and independent mutant fates (Kimura), fixed fitnesses and haploid inheritance (Fisher), equal fecundity and a 1:1 sex ratio (Maynard Smith) are assumptions written in the module header, not conclusions. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the paper is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/mutations.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/Delphi/Audit.lean> .
}

